      "title": "Lua: Don't export symbols for DLLs on Win32",
      "message": "Lua: Don't export symbols for DLLs on Win32\n\nWe don't build these libraries as DLLs, and we load them via\nluaL_requiref directly in our code so we don't need to export\nthe open symbols with __declspec(dllexport) on Windows so that\nLua can import them via the DLL. Just leave them with extern\nlinkage. That's what LUALIB_API evaluates to on non-Win32, or\non Win32 when LUA_BUILD_AS_DLL is not defined. Our other package\ndefined LUA_BUILD_AS_DLL when building the Lua DLL itself, but\nit was not defined when building Wireshark so the functions were\nextern. The vcpkg Lua distribution effectively unconditionally sets\nLUA_BUILD_AS_DLL in its luaconf.h, but we're not building DLLs.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-08-03T08:22:55.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2026-08-03T08:56:18.000-04:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/1e07b34bc55fb9f256c9728a447ec1a93abb2048"
    },
